Title: Nick and Me
Credit: Written by
Author: Author
Source: Adapted from book
Draft date: 7/30/2026

FADE IN:

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - DAY

A modest fifth-floor brick apartment in Milwaukee. The early morning light cuts through smudged windows. The atmosphere is heavy with history. 

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Nick was the guy everyone feared – rough, scarred, with a presence like a modern-day Viking... and yet, a paradox of protection and torment.

On the worn sofa, MA, a tired but loving woman with greying hair, fusses over early medications while a hulking figure, NICK, looms at the doorway. His unruly reddish-brown hair and scarred face hint at a lifetime of brawls.

MA
(softly, concerned)
Better take your pills on time, dear.

NICK
(gruffly, with a nod)
I’m watching over you, Ma.

The NARRATOR, a lean man in his early twenties with quiet eyes full of both admiration and resentment, watches them from behind a table piled with old family photos.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I grew up under Nick’s shadow – a protector, a bully, and the man I both adored and despised.

EXT. DOWNTOWN MILWAUKEE ALLEY / OUTSIDE A PIZZERIA - EVENING

Neon lights flicker as a modest pizzeria buzzes with late-day energy. Passersby shift aside as NICK strides in; his heavy presence forces people to move. The NARRATOR, carrying groceries, steps outside with a resigned smile.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Ma and I slogged through life with Nick’s brute strength carrying the load – until one day, when fate introduced someone different.

A young woman in a simple, black V-neck tee and jeans bumps into the NARRATOR on the sidewalk.

NARRATOR
(startled, genuine)
Are you okay?

YOUNG WOMAN (SIONNA)
(smiling lightly)
Yes… my name is Sionna.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In that brief moment of collision, my world tilted. Something in her gentle eyes promised a different path.

INT. THE JAVA HUT COFFEE SHOP - DAY

Sunlight filters through tall windows in the cozy coffee shop. NARRATOR and SIONNA sit at a small table with steaming coffees and a copy of “Wuthering Heights” between them.

SIONNA
(reading softly)
“You never see everything…” Sometimes literature feels like a gateway to our hidden selves.

NARRATOR
(earnest)
I’ve never felt so understood. You make me see ideas—and perhaps a better future.

They share a warm, knowing smile as ambient jazz underscores their connection.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
There, over coffee and literature, I found solace—a spark that challenged a lifetime defined by my brother’s storm.

INT. APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

The apartment is dark except for a single table lamp. MA sits confused, repeating lines about missing her pain pills. The NARRATOR paces anxiously. NICK enters sharply, anger simmering beneath his gravelly tone.

NICK
(angry, accusing)
You let Ma’s affairs slip! How can you be so careless?

NARRATOR
(defensive)
I did what I could—she’s just… tired and confused.

A tense silence falls. The conflict between duty and resentment simmers in the air.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
That night, the cracks in our fragile world deepened. I began to wonder if love and loyalty could truly outweigh the cost of living under his tyrannical shadow.

INT. HOSPITAL WAITING ROOM - DAY

Fluorescent lights hum over a sparse waiting area. A worried NARRATOR clutches a phone displaying missed calls. A DOCTOR enters, somber.

DOCTOR
Your mother’s blood pressure is dangerously high. We must admit her immediately.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In our world, every crisis carried an avalanche of other crises. Ma’s failing health, Nick’s unpredictable rage… and my growing isolation.

A phone message from OFFICER DUPUIS plays as the NARRATOR listens, dread in his eyes.

OFFICER DUPUIS (V.O.)
Mr. Olson, please come to the station regarding a family incident.

The NARRATOR’s face pales. He steps out, burdened by an inescapable guilt.

INT. NARRATOR APARTMENT - NIGHT

The apartment is a tomb of scattered papers and memories. MA lies silent on a chair—empty eyes and a vacant smile. The NARRATOR cradles her now lifeless hand, tears streaming down his face. His phone buzzes with angry texts. A flash of violent confrontation with NICK plays in his mind.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In the chaos that followed—a tragic accident seared into my heart—Ma was gone. And the bitter truth that Nick’s reckless indulgence had cost us everything emerged with ruthless clarity.

A brief, raw flashback: NICK, enraged, shouting obscenities; the clatter of a struggle; a heavy silence descending after a fatal blow.

NARRATOR (V.O.) (CONT’D)
I was left with guilt, grief, and a burning resolve to free myself from his control.

INT. APARTMENT HALLWAY - NIGHT

In a dim corridor, NARRATOR confronts NICK. Emotions boil over as they exchange heated words. Physical struggle ensues; the camera focuses on clenched fists and a gleaming switchblade. 

NARRATOR
(shouting, anguished)
You killed her, Nick! You’ve stolen our past—and our future!

NICK
(bitter, remorseful)
I’ve been lost in my own darkness... but you always had a way of judging me.

After a brief, brutal scuffle that ends without further bloodshed, NARRATOR staggers away, battered eyes determined.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In that moment, I vowed to reclaim my life—no longer defined by his shadow or my own sorrow.

MONTAGE – VARIOUS LOCATIONS – DAY

– The NARRATOR attending college classes, furrowing his brow over textbooks in a quiet library.
– Late nights studying, intercut with moments at a busy pizza parlor where he learns to toss dough with practiced ease.
– A growing romance with SIONNA: shared smiles over park bench walks and gentle touches in a warmly lit apartment.
– Newspaper headlines blur: “Accident Shakes Family” and “Nick Olson in Legal Trouble.”

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Slowly, the bitterness gave way to a new me—a man who forged his path through education, hard work, and the healing light of love.

INT. PRISON VISITATION ROOM - DAY

A drab, double-locked room with sterile fluorescent lighting. NARRATOR sits across a thick glass window from NICK, now gaunt and subdued in prison attire.

NICK
(hoarsely)
Little brother... I never thought I’d see you here.

NARRATOR
(calm, resolute)
I’m here to say goodbye to the man I once resented—and to forgive. I forgive you, Nick. I have to let go of the past to live in the present.

A heavy silence passes as NICK’s eyes glisten with remorse.

NICK
(whispering)
Thank you... I’m... I’m sorry.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In that room, I found closure. Though our bond was marred by tragedy, forgiveness freed me from a lifetime of shame.

EXT. SEATTLE STREET - DAY

A vibrant urban street in Seattle under a bright sky. The NARRATOR, now confident and mature, strides along with a calm smile. Neon signs and bustling cafés frame the scene.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Time moved on, and with it came growth, opportunity—and even hope. My pain transformed into purpose.

A quick series of shots showing:
– The NARRATOR overseeing a busy pizza parlor named “Tony’s Boy’s Pizza.”
– Him sharing quiet moments with SIONNA in a sunlit park.
– A newspaper headline reading “President Olson: From Struggle to Success.”

NARRATOR (V.O.) (CONT’D)
I learned that forgiving the past lets you write a new future. I became who I am today—a man no longer imprisoned by grief nor defined by anger.

INT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

SIONNA and the NARRATOR sit together, sharing soft laughter over a cinnamon roll. Their eyes meet with understanding and renewal.

SIONNA
(quietly)
You’ve finally found your light.

NARRATOR
(smiling warmly)
For us, for our family… for me.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In every ending, there is a new beginning. I embraced love, shed old burdens, and moved forward with hope.

EXT. SEATTLE SKYLINE - SUNSET

The city glows in the fading light as the NARRATOR stands on a balcony overlooking the skyline. He looks peaceful, reflective, and resolute.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
This is my story—a journey of pain, betrayal, and ultimate forgiveness. I now stand free, ready to write the next chapter of my life.

FADE OUT / THE END
